ed jurisdictions, other prohibited uses of the website and the governing law. Kindly amend.","notes":null},{"title":"Terms & Conditions","tag":"Operations","criticality":"Critical","due":"2025-05-15","description":"The registered domain must make available to players the T&Cs of the site, which must include at minimum the procedure for the closure of the player accounts, the procedure for the lodging of complaints, the prohibited jurisdictions, other prohibited uses of the website and the governing law. Kindly amend.","notes":null},{"title":"Responsible Gaming","tag":"Operations","criticality":"Critical","due":"2025-05-15","description":"The registered domain must make available to its players a Responsible Gaming policy which must include at minimum the procedure for self-exclusion, any deposit/loss limits available and links to problem gambling organisations. Kindly amend.","notes":null},{"title":"Player Registration","tag":"Player Registration","criticality":"Critical","due":"2025-05-15","description":"The registration form does not require the players’ address or DOB. This information must be collected at the latest prior to the first deposit. Kindly amend.","notes":null},{"title":"Prohibited Jurisdictions","tag":"Prohibiited Countries","criticality":"Critical","due":"2025-05-15","description":"The registered domain allows players to register an account while accessing the site from a Netherlands IP address. Furthermore, the registration form allows players to register an account by choosing Curacao or the Netherlands as their country of residence. Players residing in Curacao, the Netherlands (and any country forming part of the kingdom of the Netherlands), USA, UN sanctioned countries and FATF blacklisted countries must not be allowed to register an account. Kindly amend.","notes":null},{"title":"Crypto Exchange","tag":"Operations","criticality":"Critical","due":"2025-05-15","description":"The registered domain appears to require players to deposit via cryptocu